Z||000125||stimpy||03-04-2001||10:34 AM||||Johnny, ponder this. You feel it is absurd to have faith in the invisible.  Yet every day, hundreds of thousands of times, you put faith in things unseen merely by drawing breath. Truely, one can never be absolutely sure that their next breath may not be made up of some toxic gas that could kill you instantly. If you think that is absurdist thinking, think Bhopal, India. Think Chernobyl.  Hell, think Richmond, CA.<P>People breath because they need to breath. People have faith because they need to. It's how we're wired together. If we required absolute proof on everything, we would become prisoners of our own skepticism. And before rayb calls me a bible tumpre one more time, let me clearly state that I believe God to be accessible to all. I believe as long as we purely seek God in our hearts, we shall find God. <BR> <BR>||||reg||1
